<http://data.silknow.org/object/2b323cef-9307-3ddc-bb6e-a1d3530cae21/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Forehead cloth of embroidered linen with coloured silks, silver and silver-gilt threads in detached buttonhole stitch, chain stitch, plaited braid stitch and couching. The pattern consists of rows of strawberries and caterpillars repeating with peacocks and roses with rosehips. The embroidery is unfinished at the edges, and traces of original pen and ink drawing remain along with the triangular outline. The forehead cloth is unlined and the hemming of the edges are modern. The thread count is approximately 65 x 80 threads per inch."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/2b323cef-9307-3ddc-bb6e-a1d3530cae21> .

